    "created_at": "2020-10-01T18:26:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-10-01T18:26:23Z",
    "body": "@tabatkins didn't want to fix a somewhat more general problem in https://github.com/tabatkins/bikeshed/issues/1327, but maybe this subset is easier. Respec can probably use the same syntax, but would also need the implementation change.\r\n\r\nHowever, I do think that specs are easier to read when the call sites look like the definitions, and systematically using one grammatical form for definitions but a different one for calls violates that. I'm not at all tied to changing the definitions: I'd be happy if we could find a way to use the infinitives at the call sites if we can find a way to make that read well.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
